# Template of the .env file.
# Copy it to a file called exactly .env (with the dot, without ".example") in the project folder,
# and write the values after the equals sign, without spaces and without quotes.
# The .env file is ignored by git: keys and addresses stay on your computer.
# Never paste keys in chats, notebooks or commits. If you shared them by mistake, generate new ones.

# News (uv run python -m src.news). Keys are generated at https://alpaca.markets: free account, Paper Trading, API Keys panel,
# Generate New Keys. The Secret Key is shown only once. The steps are in src/README.md, step 4.
ALPACA_API_KEY_ID=
ALPACA_API_SECRET_KEY=

# News agent (uv run python -m src.agent_variants.agent). The model runs locally behind a server compatible with the OpenAI API.
# AGENT_BASE_URL: address of the server. Empty = http://localhost:1234/v1 (LM Studio on this computer). Ollama: http://localhost:11434/v1.
#                 If the model runs on another computer: http://<address of that computer>:<port>/v1
# AGENT_MODEL:    name of the model as the server calls it (in LM Studio: `lms ls`; in Ollama: `ollama list`).
# AGENT_API_KEY:  only if the server asks for one; for a local server it stays empty.
AGENT_BASE_URL=
AGENT_MODEL=
AGENT_API_KEY=
